1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,540
Last time, we learned to make big numbers using more than one rod.

2
00:00:05,240 --> 00:00:08,800
Today, we're going back to one rod to learn something new.

3
00:00:09,420 --> 00:00:11,320
We're going to take numbers away.

4
00:00:12,440 --> 00:00:14,680
Taking away is the opposite of adding.

5
00:00:15,400 --> 00:00:18,540
When we added, we pushed beads towards the beam.

6
00:00:19,300 --> 00:00:23,180
So when we take away, we push beads away from the beam.

7
00:00:23,720 --> 00:00:24,800
That's the whole idea.

8
00:00:25,440 --> 00:00:26,940
The rest is just practice.

9
00:00:28,200 --> 00:00:31,740
There's one more thing that changes, your finger.

10
00:00:32,560 --> 00:00:35,880
When we add, the thumb pushes the lower beads up.

11
00:00:36,600 --> 00:00:40,640
When we take away, your index finger pushes them back down.

12
00:00:41,500 --> 00:00:43,420
Let's try four, take away two.

13
00:00:44,200 --> 00:00:45,680
First, make four.

14
00:00:46,360 --> 00:00:48,620
Push four lower beads up to the beam.

15
00:00:49,320 --> 00:00:50,900
The rod is showing four.

16
00:00:51,680 --> 00:00:52,860
Now take away two.

17
00:00:53,580 --> 00:00:55,700
Push two lower beads back down.

18
00:00:55,700 --> 00:00:58,760
Two beads have moved away from the beam.

19
00:00:59,560 --> 00:01:02,160
Two lower beads are still touching the beam.

20
00:01:03,020 --> 00:01:05,400
So four, take away two, is two.

21
00:01:06,360 --> 00:01:08,960
Now let's try eight, take away three.

22
00:01:09,800 --> 00:01:11,280
First, make eight.

23
00:01:12,200 --> 00:01:14,160
Push the upper bead down for five.

24
00:01:14,800 --> 00:01:17,520
Then push three lower beads up for three.

25
00:01:18,360 --> 00:01:20,220
Five and three is eight.

26
00:01:21,220 --> 00:01:22,420
Now take away three.

27
00:01:23,160 --> 00:01:25,500
Push three lower beads back down.

28
00:01:26,020 --> 00:01:28,180
The upper bead doesn't move at all.

29
00:01:28,860 --> 00:01:31,660
Only the lower beads move away from the beam.

30
00:01:32,440 --> 00:01:34,680
The upper bead is still worth five.

31
00:01:35,520 --> 00:01:37,680
So eight, take away three, is five.

32
00:01:39,080 --> 00:01:40,720
Here's the rule so far.

33
00:01:41,380 --> 00:01:46,160
If you only need to move lower beads, just push them away from the beam.

34
00:01:47,320 --> 00:01:49,520
Now what if we need to take away five?

35
00:01:50,240 --> 00:01:52,340
Five lives on the upper bead.

36
00:01:53,040 --> 00:01:54,700
So the upper bead has to move.

37
00:01:55,460 --> 00:01:57,840
Let's try five, take away five.

38
00:01:58,520 --> 00:02:00,220
First, make five.

39
00:02:00,800 --> 00:02:02,180
Push the upper bead down.

40
00:02:02,900 --> 00:02:04,500
The rod is showing five.

41
00:02:05,340 --> 00:02:06,740
Now take away five.

42
00:02:07,300 --> 00:02:08,900
Push the upper bead back up.

43
00:02:09,560 --> 00:02:11,840
Every bead is away from the beam.

44
00:02:12,620 --> 00:02:14,880
So five, take away five, is zero.

45
00:02:16,460 --> 00:02:18,920
Let's try seven, take away five.

46
00:02:19,380 --> 00:02:20,920
First, make seven.

47
00:02:21,720 --> 00:02:23,740
Push the upper bead down for five.

48
00:02:24,360 --> 00:02:26,980
Then push two lower beads up for two.

49
00:02:27,780 --> 00:02:29,300
Now take away five.

50
00:02:29,900 --> 00:02:31,560
Push the upper bead back up.

51
00:02:32,180 --> 00:02:34,240
The two lower beads don't move.

52
00:02:34,920 --> 00:02:36,420
They're still touching the beam.

53
00:02:37,200 --> 00:02:39,540
So seven, take away five, is two.

54
00:02:40,940 --> 00:02:44,220
Sometimes both kinds of beads have to move.

55
00:02:44,780 --> 00:02:46,840
Let's try nine, take away eight.

56
00:02:47,920 --> 00:02:49,180
First, make nine.

57
00:02:49,960 --> 00:02:53,520
Push the upper bead down and all four lower beads up.

58
00:02:54,200 --> 00:02:55,580
Now take away eight.

59
00:02:56,280 --> 00:02:57,920
Eight is five and three.

60
00:02:58,620 --> 00:02:59,660
So we move both.

61
00:03:00,540 --> 00:03:03,120
First, push three lower beads down.

62
00:03:03,860 --> 00:03:05,560
Then push the upper bead up.

63
00:03:06,440 --> 00:03:08,880
One lower bead is still touching the beam.

64
00:03:08,880 --> 00:03:11,720
So nine, take away eight is one.

65
00:03:12,680 --> 00:03:14,200
Now it's your turn.

66
00:03:14,700 --> 00:03:17,720
Make nine on your own abacus and take away four.

67
00:03:18,320 --> 00:03:19,540
What number is left?

68
00:03:21,640 --> 00:03:23,840
Nine, take away four is five.

69
00:03:24,480 --> 00:03:25,140
Great job.

70
00:03:26,160 --> 00:03:30,120
Now try taking away some small numbers on your own abacus.

71
00:03:30,460 --> 00:03:34,540
If you enjoyed this video, please like and subscribe for more.

72
00:03:35,240 --> 00:03:39,140
Search for abacus kids on the Apple App Store or Google Play.

73
00:03:39,840 --> 00:03:40,900
Download it free.

74
00:03:41,480 --> 00:03:46,640
See you in the next video where we'll add and take away on two rods together.
